{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LANDED as change 1070, merged to main (commit b91cda9b3).\n\nThe fixture now asserts BOTH halves of the virginity invariant:\n  conftest.py:86   assert rebar.list_tickets() == []   (inside the MonkeyPatch context)\n  conftest.py:103  assert not (repo / '.rebar').exists()\n\nPlacement was forced, not stylistic: the tickets check needs REBAR_ROOT and cwd pinned at the template, and the post-build assertions at :103 run AFTER the MonkeyPatch context exits. That is why the .rebar check can be a plain filesystem test at :103 and this one cannot.\n\nProven load-bearing before push, per the Testing section: seeding a ticket into the template build made the fixture raise 'template must be built with no tickets'; removing the seed returned tests/interfaces to 1397 passed / 12 skipped — identical to before the change, satisfying the 'same collected/passed counts' criterion. make lint and make typecheck clean.\n\nWhy this was worth its own change rather than an evidence comment on 699f: a test-level check only protects runs that SELECT that test, so a narrowed 'pytest tests/interfaces/store' had no protection at all. Asserting at construction fires once per worker before any test runs and covers every consumer."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785455715089883001,"uuid":"8f1f053f-f0dd-45fd-8396-3ba3800ce04b"}